a-sindhu-para/","title":"Ke Yābi Ke Yābi Bhāi?"}}},"song":{"meta":{"page":137,"author":"Śrīla Premānanda Dās","first_line":"emana gaurāṅga vine nāhi āra"},"title":["Emana Gaurāṅga Vine Nāhi Āra"],"author":["by Śrīla Premānanda Dās"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["    emana gaurāṅga vine nāhi āra","hena avatāra    habe ki hayechhe","    hena prema parachāra"],"translation":["No one is like Lord Gaurāṅga! Will there ever be an incarnation like Him, an incarnation that preached ecstatic love of Godhead as He did?"],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["duramati ati    patita pāṣaṇḍī","    prāṇe nā mārila kāre","hari-nāma diye    hṛdaya śodhila","    yāchi giyā ghare ghare"],"translation":["He did not kill the fallen wicked-hearted blasphemers. Instead, He went from house to house visiting them. He begged them to chant Lord Kṛṣṇa’s Holy Names. He gave them the Holy Names and purified their hearts."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["bhava-viriñchira    vāñchhita ye prema","    jagate phelila ḍhāli","    (bhava viriñchi yā vāñchhā kare)","kāṅgale pāiye    khāila nāchiye","    bājāiye karatāli"],"translation":["To the world He freely gave the rare gift of ecstatic love of Godhead, a gift even Brahmā and Śiva attain only with great difficulty. Attaining that gift, the poor people of this world danced and clapped their hands."],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["hāsiye kā̐diye    preme gaḍāgaḍi","    pulake vyāpila aṅga","chaṇḍāle brāhmaṇe    kare kolākuli","    kabe vā chhila e raṅga"],"translation":["They laughed and wept. Overcome with ecstasy, they rolled on the ground. The hairs of their bodies stood erect. The brāhmaṇas and chaṇḍālas embraced. There was great bliss."],"isLong":false},{"number":"5","text":["ḍākiye hā̐kiye    khola-karatāle","    gāiye dhāiye phire","dekhiyā śamana    tarāsa pāiye","    kapāṭa hānila dvāre"],"translation":["Loudly they called out the Holy Names, playing the mṛdaṅga and karatāls. They sang, ran, and danced in a circle. Seeing all this, peaceful composure became afraid, fled, and knocked on people’s doors."],"isLong":false},{"number":"6","text":["e tina bhuvana    ānande bharila","    uṭhila maṅgala-sora","kahe premānanda    emana gaurāṅge","    rati nā janmila mora"],"translation":["An auspicious tumult arose. The three worlds were filled with bliss. Premānanda says: “Alas! Attachment for Lord Gaurāṅga did not arise in me.”"],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/emona-gauranga-bine-nahi-ara","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":"https://telegra.ph/Emona-Gaurāṅga-bine-nāhi-āra-02-22"},"head":{"canonical":"/en/emona-gauranga-bine-nahi-ara/","description":"Emana Gaurāṅga Vine Nāhi Āra — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Premānanda Dās with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Emana Gaurāṅga Vine Nāhi Āra. by Śrīla Premānanda Dās | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en","slug":"emona-gauranga-bine-nahi-ara"}}